<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26414" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίδημι</span></b> , 
			Aeol.
		
		inf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίδην</span> and pres. ind. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίδει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			, part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διδείς, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εῖσα</span>,
					<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έν</span>,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				2156
			</span></i>, al. (Delph.), fem. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ[ιδέ]ουσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Delph.</u>
					3(2).131
				</span></i>
			: redupl. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέω</span>
				(A):—<i>bind, fetter,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥ ποτ᾽ Ἀχιλλεὺς . . δίδη μόσχοισι
				λύγοισιν</span> (
				Ep.
			
			<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>
			impf. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐδίδη</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.105
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δέ σ᾽ . . ἐν δεσμοῖσι
				διδέντων</span> (<i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεόντων</span>) <i>let them
				bind</i> thee, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.54
			</span></i>: 3pl. ind. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διδέᾱσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					5.8.24
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεσμεύουσι</span>
			).</div>
